Third-party and source materials
--------------------------------

1. Sanskrit base texts. The stotras published here are ancient
   compositions in the public domain. The Śrī Durgā Saptaślokī is a
   selection from the Durgā Saptaśatī (Devī Māhātmya) of the
   Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa.

2. Electronic transcriptions. The romanized text of the Śrī Durgā
   Saptaślokī was keyed from shlokam.org, which states no license for
   its transcription. See SOURCES.md §1.2 for the full provenance
   statement, the licensing analysis, and the resulting block on
   commercial redistribution. Every correction, normalization, and
   emendation applied to the received text is logged in SOURCES.md
   §§1.3–1.6.

3. Fonts. None are bundled or fetched. All files use fonts already
   present on the reader's operating system. See SOURCES.md §2.

4. Third-party code. None. See SOURCES.md §3.

